    "source_commit": "a3e4951ea6a0477b784c27c1dcbfd9c130878c5a",
    "tool": "go-pmtiles"
  },
  "what_this_is": "(z,x,y) to PMTiles v3 Hilbert tile id. Every tile_id is the return value of pmtiles.ZxyToID from the pinned go-pmtiles source. Nothing here was computed by hand or from a reading of the spec.",
  "why_this_is_here": "The suite carries a second, independent implementation of the PMTiles Hilbert curve, in tests/common/pmtiles.rs, so it can say which cells a wrong convention would move. A copy of the code under test could not answer that: it would report that nothing moves. But a second implementation asserted correct is not a second implementation shown correct, and corrupting its `correct` branch left every test in the suite green. These rows are what pin it, and they pin `libviprs::pmtiles::zxy_to_tileid` to the same numbers at the same time."
}
